1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"phase-6--6b-vocabulary-gaps","kind":"phase-article","route":"/roadmap/phase-6/6b-vocabulary-gaps","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/phase-6/6b-vocabulary-gaps","sourceHash":"47143ffb707d3f95f82c93c1fe18b1719bcb4efcff23e0ce199edf1fa8179a83","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:12:03.721Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"6B — Vocabulary Gaps","zh":"6B——词汇缺口"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"what-youre-doing","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What You're Doing","zh":"你正在做什么"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You're fluent in many domains, but you've probably noticed gaps — topics where you suddenly can't find the right sausage, situations where you know exactly what you want to say but don't know how.","zh":"你在许多领域都已经能够流利交流，但可能也注意到了自己的缺口——有些话题中，你突然找不到合适的表达；有些情况下，你明明清楚自己想说什么，却不知道该怎么说。"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Every learner experiences this. You've learned a LOT of words, around 6000-7000, but a native adult knows 15,000-20,000+, and the missing words tend to be the ones that come up in everyday life just often enough to know, but not in books or TV shows. Or specialized vocabulary related to specific fields.","zh":"每个学习者都会经历这种情况。你已经学会了很多词，大约 6000—7000 个，但成年母语者掌握 15000—20000 个甚至更多，而缺失的词往往正是日常生活中出现频率刚好足够让人认识、却不常出现在书籍或电视节目里的词。也可能是与特定领域相关的专业词汇。"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This sub-phase is about actively hunting down and filling those gaps. It's less about learning passively from content and more about using content to find what you're missing, then targeting those areas.","zh":"这个子阶段的目标，是主动找出并填补这些缺口。重点不再是从内容中被动学习，而是利用内容发现自己缺少什么，然后针对性地学习。"}},{"id":"whats-new","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What's New","zh":"有什么新内容"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Targeted domain expansion</strong> — Deliberately immerse in content from domains you've avoided or underexplored. If you've mostly watched dramas, try cooking shows, sports commentary, or news. If you've mostly read fiction, try non-fiction, opinion pieces, or technical writing in a field you know. Each new domain surfaces vocabulary you've been missing. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/domains\">Domains</a>","zh":"<strong>针对性扩展领域</strong>——有意识地沉浸于你过去回避或探索不足的领域内容。如果你主要看剧情剧，试试烹饪节目、体育解说或新闻。如果你主要读小说，试试非虚构作品、评论文章，或你熟悉领域的技术写作。每个新领域都会呈现出你过去缺少的词汇。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/domains\">领域</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Read books</strong> — Okay. I'll say it again. If you aren't reading novels, start doing it. You'll thank me later. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/extensive-reading\">Extensive Reading</a>","zh":"<strong>阅读书籍</strong>——好吧，我再说一遍。如果你还没有读小说，就开始读吧。以后你会感谢我的。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/extensive-reading\">广泛阅读</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Video Creation</strong> — Creating content in the target language is an excellent way to discover vocabulary gaps. When you try to explain something and can't find the right word, you've found a gap. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/video-creation\">Video Creation</a>","zh":"<strong>视频创作</strong>——用目标语言创作内容，是发现词汇缺口的绝佳方式。当你试图解释某件事，却找不到合适的词时，你就发现了一个缺口。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/video-creation\">视频创作</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Topic Talk and Topic Writing</strong> — Repeated practice talking/writing about specific domains. Choose topics deliberately — things you w<em>ant to</em> be able to discuss but currently can't. Household items, medical situations, financial terminology, sports, food, relationships, workplace dynamics. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/topic-talk\">Topic Talk</a> <a href=\"/roadmap/library/topic-writing\">Topic Writing</a>","zh":"<strong>主题口语与主题写作</strong>——反复练习围绕特定领域进行口头或书面表达。有意识地选择主题——选择那些你<em>想要</em>能够讨论、但目前还无法讨论的内容。家居用品、医疗情况、金融术语、体育、食物、人际关系、职场互动。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/topic-talk\">主题口语</a> <a href=\"/roadmap/library/topic-writing\">主题写作</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Sentence Mining returns.</strong> You used sentence mining heavily in Phase 2 to build core vocabulary. Now it's back, but targeted at specific domains and the \"uncommon but useful\" words that round out your vocabulary. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/sentence-mining\">Sentence Mining</a>","zh":"<strong>句子挖掘回来了。</strong>你在第 2 阶段大量使用句子挖掘来建立核心词汇。现在它再次登场，但目标是特定领域，以及那些“并不常见却很有用”、能够完善你词汇量的词。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/sentence-mining\">句子挖掘</a>"}},{"id":"your-routine","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Your Routine","zh":"你的日常安排"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Priming increases as vocabulary study becomes more important again: <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">The Pillars of Language Learning</a>","zh":"随着词汇学习再次变得重要，预热所占比例也会提高：<a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">语言学习的支柱</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"<strong>Priming:</strong> 20%","zh":"<strong>预热：</strong>20%"},{"en":"<strong>Interactive Immersion:</strong> 30%","zh":"<strong>互动式沉浸：</strong>30%"},{"en":"<strong>Freeflow Immersion:</strong> 20%","zh":"<strong>自由流沉浸：</strong>20%"},{"en":"<strong>Output:</strong> 30%","zh":"<strong>输出：</strong>30%"}]},{"id":"sample-daily-schedule","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"Sample Daily Schedule","zh":"每日安排示例"}},{"id":"segment-0015","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Vocab study: 20 mins","zh":"词汇学习：20 分钟"},{"en":"Sentence Mining: 30 mins","zh":"句子挖掘：30 分钟"},{"en":"Freeflow Reading: 20 mins","zh":"自由流阅读：20 分钟"},{"en":"Video Creation or Topic Talk: 30 mins","zh":"视频创作或主题口语：30 分钟"}]},{"id":"when-to-move-on","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Move On","zh":"何时进入下一阶段"}},{"id":"segment-0017","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Move to 6C when you:","zh":"当你满足以下条件时，进入 6C："}},{"id":"segment-0018","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Know 8000+ words","zh":"掌握 8000 个以上的词"},{"en":"Can discuss a wide range of everyday topics — anything a high school graduate would be comfortable talking about — without getting stuck on missing vocabulary","zh":"能够讨论广泛的日常话题——任何高中毕业生都能自在谈论的话题——而不会因为缺少词汇而卡住"}]},{"id":"research-and-reasoning","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Research and Reasoning","zh":"研究与依据"}},{"id":"segment-0020","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The focus on expanding vocabulary at this stage is supported by <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.3138/cmlr.63.1.59\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Nation's (2006)</a> research on vocabulary size and lexical coverage. Nation found that the most frequent 2,000 word families cover roughly 80% of everyday text, but reaching comfortable unassisted comprehension requires far more: approximately 8,000–9,000 word families for 98% coverage of written text, and 6,000–7,000 for spoken text. At 98% coverage, unknown words become rare enough that readers can infer their meaning from context — this is the threshold where vocabulary stops being a bottleneck for fluent comprehension.","zh":"现阶段强调扩展词汇，得到了<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.3138/cmlr.63.1.59\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Nation（2006）</a>关于词汇量和词汇覆盖率研究的支持。Nation 发现，最常见的 2000 个词族大约覆盖日常文本的 80%，但要达到舒适的无辅助理解，还需要更多词汇：书面文本需要约 8000—9000 个词族才能达到 98% 的覆盖率，口语文本则需要 6000—7000 个。在 98% 的覆盖率下，生词已经少到足以让读者根据上下文推断其含义——这就是词汇不再成为流利理解瓶颈的阈值。"}},{"id":"segment-0021","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The vocabulary gaps you encounter at this level correspond to what <a href=\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/learning-vocabulary-in-another-language/491314AA1B451AD04F3536000F1C9F0D\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Nation (2001)</a> described as lower-frequency but contextually important vocabulary — words outside the high-frequency core that native speakers know but don't use constantly. Because your input history inevitably skews toward certain topics and genres, these gaps tend to cluster by domain. Deliberate domain expansion is an efficient strategy precisely because it surfaces these clusters of missing vocabulary rather than isolated random words.","zh":"你在这个水平遇到的词汇缺口，正对应了<a href=\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/learning-vocabulary-in-another-language/491314AA1B451AD04F3536000F1C9F0D\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Nation（2001）</a>所描述的低频但具有语境重要性的词汇——它们不属于高频核心词汇，但母语者知道，只是不经常使用。由于你的输入经历不可避免地偏向某些话题和体裁，这些缺口往往会按领域聚集。有意识地扩展领域之所以高效，正是因为它能呈现成组的缺失词汇，而不是孤立的随机词。"}}],"cards":[]},"siteBasePath":"/my_learning_docs"}]
